  "notes": "Closed-score SATB: Soprano+Alto share the treble staff, Tenor+Bass share the bass staff. A correct conversion yields FOUR parts (Soprano, Alto, Tenor, Bass), each with its own notes; all three verses belong to the Soprano part (lyric numbers 1-3) and must stay attached to soprano notes, including melisma skips (e.g. \"pre - cious\" spans a slurred melisma). DAMAGE (photocopy-thick): Dark photocopy, 1-bit: high threshold + ink spread - noteheads fill in (half notes start to look like quarters), beams/slurs/ties merge with staff lines, lyrics thicken. scan adds toner specks and a black lid edge; severe adds -1.2 deg skew, black surround, heavy specks and pepper noise. TRUTH LIMITATIONS: Severe: some hollow (half/whole) noteheads may be visually filled; durations remain as in the truth (they are recoverable from beat counting only)."
